        "root_concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 04 The Marine Chronometer",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nLONGITUDE PROBLEM: THE GEOMETRY"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md#005",
      "path": [
        "04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:watchmaking:04-marine-chronometer, git-history:watchmaking:04-marine-chronometer]",
        "canonical_path": "watchmaking/04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md",
        "concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "current_path": "watchmaking/04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md",
        "id": "maxim:watchmaking:marine-chronometer",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "watchmaking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 04 The Marine Chronometer",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Earth's coordinate system:\n  Latitude: angle from equator (0° to ±90°)\n    → Measurable directly from altitude of sun or Polaris\n    → Sextant + almanac → latitude with ~1 nautical mile accuracy\n    → SOLVED: no clock needed"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md#006",
      "path": [
        "04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:watchmaking:04-marine-chronometer, git-history:watchmaking:04-marine-chronometer]",
        "canonical_path": "watchmaking/04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md",
        "concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "current_path": "watchmaking/04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md",
        "id": "maxim:watchmaking:marine-chronometer",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "watchmaking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 04 The Marine Chronometer",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Longitude: angle from prime meridian (0° to ±180°)\n    → Requires knowing two things SIMULTANEOUSLY:\n        1. Local time (from sun/star observation)\n        2. Time at reference meridian (Greenwich)\n    → Difference in times → angular difference → longitude\n    → 1 hour time difference = 15° longitude = ~900 nmi at equator\n    → UNSOLVED until Harrison's chronometer"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md#007",
      "path": [
        "04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:watchmaking:04-marine-chronometer, git-history:watchmaking:04-marine-chronometer]",
        "canonical_path": "watchmaking/04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md",
        "concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "current_path": "watchmaking/04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md",
        "id": "maxim:watchmaking:marine-chronometer",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "watchmaking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 04 The Marine Chronometer",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE MATH:\n  Local noon: sun transits the meridian\n  Note Greenwich Time on chronometer at local noon\n  ΔT (hours) × 15°/hour = Longitude East of Greenwich\n    (negative if chronometer shows later time = ship is west)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md#008",
      "path": [
        "04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:watchmaking:04-marine-chronometer, git-history:watchmaking:04-marine-chronometer]",
        "canonical_path": "watchmaking/04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md",
        "concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "current_path": "watchmaking/04-MARINE-CHRONOMETER.md",
        "id": "maxim:watchmaking:marine-chronometer",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "watchmaking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 04 The Marine Chronometer",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Error of 1 minute of time = 15 nautical miles of longitude at equator\n  Error of 4 minutes of time = 60 nautical miles = 1 degree of longitude\n```"
    },
