        "root_concepts": "[marine, chronometer]",
        "section": "watchmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Watchmaking - 04 The Marine Chronometer",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Harrison's insight: the problem with a portable clock at sea was not the escapement — the verge (in use since ~1280) was known — but the driving force inconsistency (mainspring torque variation), temperature effects on the balance spring, and the ship's motion disturbing any pendulum."
    },
    {
