        "title": "Watchmaking - 04 The Marine Chronometer",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "1. TWIN BALANCED OSCILLATORS (anti-ship-motion):\n   Instead of a pendulum (disturbed by ship's motion):\n   Two interconnected brass-weighted oscillating arms\n   Moving in opposite directions simultaneously\n   Gyroscopic effect: one oscillator compensates for\n   disturbance to the other\n   → Motion of ship averages out"
    },
    {
